        "title": "Scipio Africanus",
        "raw_score": 5.839539401721678,
        "source": "kg"
      }
    },
    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_10",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "He was born in humble circumstances in Worcestershire, and educated at Exeter College, Oxford in 1621. He left the university without taking a degree, and in about 1630 began a career in London as a dramatist. He was employed at some point in the household of a nobleman near Worcester, and seems to have been of a convivial disposition. He had at least two children, Bridget and William, both of whom died within two years of his death, and were buried with him at St Giles in the Fields.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.8651457225991726,
      "temperature": 0.8651457225991726,
      "expanded": false,
